From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:23:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] leds: aw9120: turn the outputs off while the system
 sleeps

Each lit output draws milliamps, and nothing turns the indicators off
for a suspend. Let the LED core do it: with LED_CORE_SUSPENDRESUME it
sets every LED to zero before the chip's bus suspends and restores the
brightness at resume, through the driver's normal brightness writes.
---
 drivers/leds/rgb/leds-aw9120.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/leds/rgb/leds-aw9120.c b/drivers/leds/rgb/leds-aw9120.c
index 840194ac8..8d895c742 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/rgb/leds-aw9120.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/rgb/leds-aw9120.c
@@ -211,6 +211,8 @@ static int aw9120_register_led(struct aw9120 *chip, struct aw9120_led *led,
 	struct led_classdev *cdev = &led->mc.led_cdev;
 
 	cdev->max_brightness = LED_FULL;
+	/* Off while the system sleeps; each lit output costs milliamps */
+	cdev->flags |= LED_CORE_SUSPENDRESUME;
 
 	if (led->mc.num_colors) {
 		cdev->brightness_set_blocking = aw9120_mc_set;
-- 
